sequencer_service 0.1.0
Usage: sequencer_service [OPTIONS] <config>

Arguments:
  <config>  

Options:
  -p, --port <PORT>
          [default: 3040]
      --listen-address <LISTEN_ADDRESS>
          Interface the RPC server binds to. The RPC has no caller auth — bind loopback unless the port is firewalled [default: 0.0.0.0]
      --home <HOME>
          Override the config's home directory (`RocksDB` + bedrock signing key), so multiple instances can share one config file
      --metrics-address <METRICS_ADDRESS>
          Override the config's `metrics_address`, so multiple instances can share one config file without fighting over the exporter port
      --signing-key <SIGNING_KEY>
          File holding the 32-byte key to sign blocks with, overriding the config's `signing_key`. It is the only thing that has to differ between the sequencers of one committee, so passing it separately lets them all run off one config file
  -h, --help
          Print help
  -V, --version
          Print version
